Add the least-connections load-balance strategy.
Based on upstream PR: https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/pull/3328
Source commit: 878bf4bf900f6eab0dd1d51b0f67dc7cc3e20607

Reserve a member when a TCP/UDP dial starts and release it on dial failure or
connection close. Repeated members carry proportionate shares; dead members
are skipped, ties rotate and Unwrap reports without reserving. Reject hash-key
for this strategy. Existing strategies keep their original selection behavior.

Keep each group's least-connections state in its strategy closure. All strategies
use the same (proxy, optional release) result; selection touch and connection
acquisition are separate flags. Strategies without connection accounting return
nil release, so their connections need no additional close wrapper.

Retain the upstream selection algorithm and cover weighted selection, TCP/UDP
lifetime, dial failures, duplicate close, pending dials, concurrent reservation
and release, member replacement, per-group isolation, Unwrap and legacy strategy
contracts. Enable explicitly with strategy: least-connections; it counts
connections and does not measure throughput/latency or pin sessions.

